// This sketch intentionally contains no code and serves only as an anchor for the
// Arduino IDE. Ensure that this .ino file has the same name as the folder in which
// it is located. Additionally, the subfolder "src" must be present, as this is
// where the code and libraries are located. Settings are made in config.h.
// Then open this file in the Arduino IDE, select the board "ATmega644" (MightyCore),
// variant "644P / 644PA", clock "External 8 MHz", BOD "2.7V", EEPROM "retained",
// bootloader "No bootloader", the programmer "USBasp (MightyCore)" and click
// "Upload Using Programmer". This uploads the firmware without the SD card
// bootloader; use the makefile ("make flash") to install both.
// ===================================================================================
// To make it work, you have to install MightyCore for the Arduino IDE:
// https://github.com/MCUdude/MightyCore
// ===================================================================================
